      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Subepicardial aneurysm is a rare complication of acute myocardial infarction (AMI) and is associated with the risk of spontaneous rupture. We present two patients with subepicardial aneurysms detected after 1 day and 6 weeks after AMI. Both lesions were successfully treated by patch repair."},
